window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Everything Spontaneous in the Land of Doll Parts<br> Read by Avery Sandoval and Tara Sandoval<br> Running time: 9 hours 45 Minutes</p> <p>One morning, people simply started burning.</p> <p>No warning. No mercy. They called it SHC, Spontaneous Human Combustion, and overnight, the world collapsed into fire, ash, and fear. Anyone could ignite. Everyone learned to watch each other closely.</p> <p>The audiobook edition of Everything Spontaneous in the Land of Doll Parts delivers a haunting, intimate listening experience set in the scorched remnants of Colorado, where survival is fragile and connection is dangerous.</p> <p>Rory lives with the guilt of her mother’s death, a weight that never cools. Dante carries the echo of her father’s final scream, a sound that follows her through every quiet moment. Both women have learned how to endure alone, until the end of the world brings them together.</p> <p>What begins as survival becomes something far riskier.</p> <p>In a landscape ruled by starvation, violence, and the constant threat of spontaneous combustion, love isn’t a comfort, it’s a liability. Every attachment creates something to lose. And yet, against reason and instinct, Rory and Dante choose each other anyway.</p> <p>This audiobook is meant to be listened to closely, during long walks, late nights, and moments when silence feels heavier than sound. It’s a story about staying alive when the body can betray you at any moment, and about the quiet courage it takes to keep loving anyway.</p> <p>Everything Spontaneous in the Land of Doll Parts is a sapphic post-apocalyptic romance infused with survival horror and emotional depth. Perfect for listeners who crave LGBTQ+ dystopian fiction where love forms in the ruins and refuses to go quietly.</p> <p>When the world burns without warning, love may be the last thing you risk, and the only reason you do.</p>"; 
